jobs.description:
**Responsibilities**

1.Develop and manage client relationships across the U.S. market through regular on-site visits and follow-ups;

2. Drive the full sales cycle — lead development, product presentations, negotiations, and order follow-through — with the ability to close orders independently;

3. Coordinate with our China-based sales and supply chain teams to ensure fast, responsive order handling;

4. Report market feedback and sales progress to the Sales Director on a regular basis.

**Requirements**

1.Based in the New York metropolitan area and able to work on-site;

2. Must be authorized to work in the United States (visa sponsorship not available);

3. Proven sales experience in textiles, fabrics, or a related apparel industry, with familiarity in U.S. market client development;

4. Fluent English with the ability to conduct business communications independently;

5. Strong prospecting, negotiation, and client relationship management skills; self-driven and able to work independently;

6. Willingness to collaborate across time zones with international teams.

Pay: $120,000.00 - $180,000.00 per year

Benefits:

* Professional development assistance

Work Location: In person
